    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the `Owner` API response, computed as a Luhn check digit over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nChanges, each placed where it belongs:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility utility with a static `checkDigit(String)` method. This isolates the standard Luhn algorithm so it's reusable and doesn't clutter the mapper, matching the existing `BusinessDay` utility pattern.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the code-generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the derived field in via a `@Mapping` expression and a small `computeCheckDigit(owner)` default method delegating to `Luhn.checkDigit(...)`, consistent with how sibling derived fields (`membershipNumber`, etc.) are mapped.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
